{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat","id":634643,"title":"so my sidereal has been challenged to single combat","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-21T09:01:30-07:00","id":634643,"title":"so my sidereal has been challenged to single combat","content":"So my Sidereal has been challenged to a duel by his sifu's own sifu.<br /> <br /> That would be Suntarankal, the Crucible of Brass and Iron.<br /> <br /> Fifteenth Soul of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> <i>A Third Circle Demon.</i><br /> <br /> On the one hand, I'm running around flailing my arms wildly in panic. On the other hand, I, uh... I think I might have a <i>chance</i>.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I'm more terrified of my own predicament, or my own <i>character</i>.<br /> <br /> How long can one PC keep accumulating xp and buying goodies before the game becomes too ridiculously gonzo, anyway?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 08-21-2015, 12:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:09:12-07:00","id":634672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat#post634643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So my Sidereal has been challenged to a duel by his sifu's own sifu.<br /> <br /> That would be Suntarankal, the Crucible of Brass and Iron.<br /> <br /> Fifteenth Soul of Malfeas.<br /> <br /> <i>A Third Circle Demon.</i><br /> <br /> On the one hand, I'm running around flailing my arms wildly in panic. On the other hand, I, uh... I think I might have a <i>chance</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this supposed to be a duel to the death or like an exhibition bout/&quot;friendly&quot; sparring?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat#post634643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long can one PC keep accumulating xp and buying goodies before the game becomes too ridiculously gonzo, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a low threshold in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:24:18-07:00","id":634680,"title":"","content":"Characters in Exalted begin ridiculously gonzo. It gets worse from there. Go crazy, its one of the few games that doesnt give any fucks about how broken it is. Have fun with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/779-nusoardgraphite","name":"NuSoardGraphite","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar779_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:33:06-07:00","id":634699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I, uh... I think I might have a <i>chance</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will you have time to power up before the duel starts?<br /> <br /> It's been awhile, but I ran a bunch of 2e Sidereal games, and one of the things that often frustrated my players is that if they got into a fight without their form charms and/or other &quot;scenelong reality bullshit&quot; (their words, not mine) powers already turned on, it could take an inconvenient and possibly<i> deadly </i>amount of time to actually get to full combat effectiveness. That's what Avoidance Kata is for, of course, but you'd look really silly walking into a duel and then using Avoidance Kata.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:36:13-07:00","id":634715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634672#post634672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this supposed to be a duel to the death or like an exhibition bout/&quot;friendly&quot; sparring?</div> </div> </div> </div>Unclear. Sun wants to test his student's teaching methods, and his demeanor is &quot;affable yet incredi\u00e7bly threatening&quot; with a possibly sadistic streak. It's unclear whether he intends to leave my character dead, merely broken/humiliated as a painful proxy lesson to his sifu, or to test his abilities and possibly teach him something in return. Possibly a combination of those.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634672#post634672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a low threshold in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>I may or may not have 750xp and mastered three Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634699#post634699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will you have time to power up before the duel starts?<br /> <br /> It's been awhile, but I ran a bunch of 2e Sidereal games, and one of the things that often frustrated my players is that if they got into a fight without their form charms and/or other &quot;scenelong reality bullshit&quot; (their words, not mine) powers already turned on, it could take an inconvenient and possibly<i> deadly </i>amount of time to actually get to full combat effectiveness. That's what Avoidance Kata is for, of course, but you'd look really silly walking into a duel and then using Avoidance Kata.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hehehe.<br /> <br /> Yeah, I wholeheartedly agree. Power up times are a plague on Exalted character, and can make even a high-level character a cakewalk for a much less powerful ones if they don't have the right Charms on. My group has run into this a lot, and it once caused us to rout and run madly from a fight we might otherwise have been able to win.<br /> <br /> But then again... Wait, what's this?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">ASSUMING THE MAIDEN\u2019S MANTLE</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Cost</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> 1ahl; </span></span><b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mins</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>: </b>Martial Arts 6, Essence 6; </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">T<b>ype</b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Simple (Speed 5, DV -0)</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keywords</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>: </b>Combo-OK, Obvious</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Duration</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>:</b> Instant</span></span><br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Prerequisite Charms</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>: </b>Where All Roads End</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>One hand on her sword and about to strike.</i></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The barest branch is beautiful, one moment - while it breaks. At the end of his journey, in the place beyond worlds, the seeker finds that the universe as only one shape - that of his own reflection. This is not the last step on the path of revelation; first he must embrace this image and accepts what he has become - the maiden who waits at the end of all men\u2019s roads, and at the end of the world also. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The cost of this Charm must be paid upon rolling Join Battle, inflicting one point of aggravated damage on the user as his very Essence rebels under the strain of channeling it with such speed and power. If the martial artist wins Join Battle, he may then incur one point of Limit and use this Charm\u2019s action to activate as many Simple Charms as he desires as if they were reflexive and Combo-OK. Their cost must be paid as normal. The user\u2019s own anima is swallowed into his body, and his skin burns from within with a glow of burning Essence; his figure is warped into a grander, more terrible vision of himself. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i>Sutra:</i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> a Sidereal using this Charm may choose to take one point of Paradox rather than Limit. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":67,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","user":"Omicron","date":". 08-21-2015, 12:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:38:43-07:00","id":634718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat#post634643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How long can one PC keep accumulating XP and buying goodies before the game becomes too ridiculously gonzo, anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Forget when I checked out of the last long-running game I was in. Think it was around 350 or so. Was playing a Solar, though. Would be different for Sidereal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T09:43:46-07:00","id":634721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JimB</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634718#post634718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forget when I checked out of the last long-running game I was in. Think it was around 350 or so. Was playing a Solar, though. Would be different for Sidereal.</div> </div> </div> </div>350xp is about where my first Solar game stopped, yeah. At this point things were already getting kinda <i>weird</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:13:36-07:00","id":634825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634715#post634715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unclear. Sun wants to test his student's teaching methods, and his demeanor is &quot;affable yet incredi\u00e7bly threatening&quot; with a possibly sadistic streak. It's unclear whether he intends to leave my character dead, merely broken/humiliated as a painful proxy lesson to his sifu, or to test his abilities and possibly teach him something in return. Possibly a combination of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. I would bet not killed, if he's somewhat affable. Though that doesn't mean you might not get killed, just that it doesn't come across as that being an immediate goal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634715#post634715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may or may not have 750xp and mastered three Sidereal Martial Arts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you using 2.5 or 2e? Which SMA?<br /> <br /> Why exactly are you worried? I don't think this is going to be a fun fight to play out, because 2e combat is anti-fun, but it has the potential to be very one-sided in your favor. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634715#post634715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ASSUMING THE MAIDEN\u2019S MANTLE</div> </div> </div> </div>That's homebrew, right? At any rate, the cost is WAY too cheap. &quot;Any number of Simple Charms for 1 ahl&quot; is ridic. I'd make it 1 ahl or point of Limit <i>per Charm</i>, capped at (Essence) Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:25:37-07:00","id":634834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634825#post634825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you using 2.5 or 2e? Which SMA?</div> </div> </div> </div>2.5, all styles are homebrew. I wrote up most of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's homebrew, right? At any rate, the cost is WAY too cheap. &quot;Any number of Simple Charms for 1 ahl&quot; is ridic. I'd make it 1 ahl or point of Limit <i>per Charm</i>, capped at (Essence) Charms. </div> </div> </div>The point of the Charm is to let you not die if someone gets the drop on you with their Simple scene-longs up. If you have to pay Limit+Agg per Charm, then you can't activate enough Charms and you still die, and therefore the Charm fails to fulfill its purpose. It would therefore not be worth purchasing, because no matter how &quot;good&quot; the effect is on paper it doesn't actually help you in any way at all.<br /> <br /> I showed it to some people before and nobody blinked.<br /> <br /> It's the pre-capstone Charm of <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X7eOW3Gq4KlSflrvANKuYRBUVfWMGA4NDOM3deXd0QA/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Albicant Pursuit of Truth</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:40:31-07:00","id":634840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634834#post634834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The point of the Charm is to let you not die if someone gets the drop on you with their Simple scene-longs up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes it is worth considering whether or not things that are annoying are part of overall balance.<br /> <br /> It's been awhile, and my memory is hazy, but I seem to recall that for Exalts in general and Sidereals in particular, power-up times are a feature, not a bug. They exist specifically to give stealth-focused characters a niche, and to allow both PCs and NPCs to set up nice, tidy hits against combat monsters.<br /> <br /> Zel is right; a single health level (in 2e, where health levels mean shit because you go from zero to dead if someone so much as hits you) in order to completely bypass getting ninja'd is way, way to cheap, even with Essence 6 mins. Frankly I'd be reluctant to allow the effect at all.<br /> <br /> Then again, it doesn't really make 2e much worse than it already was, and high-essence 2e games are, like, broken in two or three different ways to begin with. So it's not the biggest of deals.<br /> <br /> You can probably mop the floor with this Demonic idiot unless it turns out that he's even more badass than Ligier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:45:19-07:00","id":634844,"title":"","content":"Power up times in the sense of spending two, maybe even three actions putting up all of your buffs and being open to attack, are a fun, tactical element of the game.<br /> <br /> There comes a time, however, when you have ten buffs to activate, and power ups are just a chore and an incredible liability that makes your character a complete binary of cakewalk-or-demigod.<br /> <br /> Also, I(A)M and its equivalents in other splats are not Combo-OK, meaning if anyone ever gets the first move against you when you don't have it up at a high level you're dead no matter what.<br /> <br /> I also think you guys seriously underestimate the kind of mojo a Third Circle has to pull.<br /> <br /> For reference, my character is roughly on par with our team's Dragon-Blood combat-wise, just with a bunch of powers specifically helping him in killing demons/creatures outside of fate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T10:57:15-07:00","id":634852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634844#post634844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Power up times in the sense of spending two, maybe even three actions putting up all of your buffs and being open to attack, are a fun, tactical element of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except when the game is rocket tag like 2e. If there were less risk, like 3e seems to be, sure it can be fun and tactical. That's not even the state of the game in 2.5. You can't have buff times if the time spent buffing isn't &quot;merely&quot; a little dangerous and makes you play with risk vs reward. When every action is deadly, there's no reasonable tactical choice. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634844#post634844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There comes a time, however, when you have ten buffs to activate, and power ups are just a chore and an incredible liability that makes your character a complete binary of cakewalk-or-demigod.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, and that is bad game design, frankly. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634844#post634844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I(A)M and its equivalents in other splats are not Combo-OK, meaning if anyone ever gets the first move against you when you don't have it up at a high level you're dead no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rocket tag is bullshit game design etc<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634844#post634844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think you guys seriously underestimate the kind of mojo a Third Circle has to pull.</div> </div> </div> </div>Versus a 750 XP elder Essence Sidereal, master of 3 SMAs? In 2.5 at best? Nah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:01:14-07:00","id":634860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634852#post634852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except when the game is rocket tag like 2e. If there were less risk, like 3e seems to be, sure it can be fun and tactical. That's not even the state of the game in 2.5. You can't have buff times if the time spent buffing isn't &quot;merely&quot; a little dangerous and makes you play with risk vs reward. When every action is deadly, there's no reasonable tactical choice.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Blows connect and are tanked regularly enough in our game that I don't really believe the accusation of rocket tag that much anymore. Sure, you can force a rocket tag situation with the right build, but it's usually rather inefficient. On the whole, I'd say in our sparring matches between PCs, about.. 25% to 33% of blows actually hit?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:01:30-07:00","id":634861,"title":"","content":"You guys really are underestimating Third Circle Demons. Like...Third Circle Demons are 'fight a full circle of E5 Exalts to a draw/kill several even in a loss.' If their writeups fail to reflect this (spoiler: they do), then they need to be buffed.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't really agree that Assuming the Maiden's Mantle is overpowered. I honestly see it more as, you know...a way to <i>not get instagibbed in an ambush because you need half an hour to power up.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zelbinnean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634852#post634852\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except when the game is rocket tag like 2e. If there were less risk, like 3e seems to be, sure it can be fun and tactical. That's not even the state of the game in 2.5. You can't have buff times if the time spent buffing isn't &quot;merely&quot; a little dangerous and makes you play with risk vs reward. When every action is deadly, there's no reasonable tactical choice.<br /> <br /> <br /> Yeah, and that is bad game design, frankly.<br /> <br /> <br /> Rocket tag is bullshit game design etc<br /> <br /> <br /> Versus a 750 XP elder Essence Sidereal, master of 3 SMAs? In 2.5 at best? Nah.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a modern game. Caps at Essence 5. SMAs aren't canon because canon SMAs are horribad broken. SMAs are 'roughly Solar Charm level, give or take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634860#post634860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blows connect and are tanked regularly enough in our game that I don't really believe the accusation of rocket tag that much anymore. Sure, you can force a rocket tag situation with the right build, but it's usually rather inefficient. On the whole, I'd say in our sparring matches between PCs, about.. 25% to 33% of blows actually hit?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Also, yeah, this is about right (I am in the game, too).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 08-21-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:30:21-07:00","id":634876,"title":"","content":"Regardless of opinions on the mechanical execution of 3cds, Suntarankal is <i>intended </i>to be an incredibly formidable martial artist. Even unarmed, he is said to be able to best &quot;whole schools of Exalted fighters singlehandedly&quot;, and he only draws his staff when things get serious.<br /> <br /> This game is homebrewed heavily throughout so you can be assured that your assumptions about the insignificance of spirits compared to Exalts are false in this case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-21-2015, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:44:29-07:00","id":634913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634861#post634861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I don't really agree that Assuming the Maiden's Mantle is overpowered. I honestly see it more as, you know...a way to <i>not get instagibbed in an ambush because you need half an hour to power up.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>If you're worried about being instagib by needing more than 1 action to power up, that's a rocket tag scenario.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634861#post634861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a modern game. Caps at Essence 5. SMAs aren't canon because canon SMAs are horribad broken. SMAs are 'roughly Solar Charm level, give or take.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634876#post634876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This game is homebrewed heavily throughout so you can be assured that your assumptions about the insignificance of spirits compared to Exalts are false in this case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then Hand asking the forum &quot;how screwed am I&quot; is pretty much pointless if Hand didn't also disclose all the house rules that could add up further in their favor (which didn't happen). All that anybody <i>not </i>in the game can go on is the RAW and disclosed house rules, of which there were none beyond a single Charm (and that single Charm is much better than any number of equivalent RAW E6 Solar Charms, I'll add).<br /> <br /> At any rate, based on the RAW (since I have no way to evaluate how your house rules tilt the game), I would bet on a 750 XP Exalt over just about any published NPC stat block in the game, as of the end of 2e with 2.5 errata. Especially a 750 XP Exalt with 2e-Solar-equivalent Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T11:52:04-07:00","id":634918,"title":"","content":"To be honest I never really intended to get into an in-depth discussion of the houserules and homebrew involved in our game (though if people on that forum would find that interesting, I can certainly oblige! I have a bunch to say about people's preconceptions and mistakes about how the balance of the game shakes out in practice, and with/without tweaks). This was really more of a &quot;fun horrible thing that is happening to my character&quot; thread, a bit of &quot;let me tell you about my cool game&quot; chatter, if you will.<br /> <br /> I was also interested in how people felt high-xp Exalts and 3CDs compared but on a more... theoretical, fluff, &quot;this is how it should be&quot; level, rather than strict mechanics.<br /> <br /> My question was never &quot;how screwed am I,&quot; it was more about at which point Exalts raise to such challenges as to make the game's stakes too ridiculous to take seriously.<br /> <br /> <i>Should </i>a Sidereal be able to defeat a 3CD whose purview is &quot;martial arts&quot; in single combat? <i>Should </i>have I a chance?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T12:46:29-07:00","id":634955,"title":"","content":"Yeah. If he's like some human scale dude. If guy didn't want to be beat up by a Sidereal martial artist, at martial arts, he should've properly been all like &quot;I'm just some big... thing... that you can't even imagine having a sensible looking martial arts duel with (seriously what are you even thinking do you have no sense of propriety?)&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T13:01:05-07:00","id":634984,"title":"","content":"I'd personally consider Suntarankal's purview to be more instruction through suffering than Martial Arts to keep with the image of him being a crucible.<br /> To me it's less &quot;can I beat him?&quot; and more &quot;what am I willing to lose in order to beat him?&quot;<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T13:33:39-07:00","id":635032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634918#post634918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My question was never &amp;quot;how screwed am I,&amp;quot; it was more about at which point Exalts raise to such challenges as to make the game's stakes too ridiculous to take seriously.<br /> <br /> <i>Should </i>a Sidereal be able to defeat a 3CD whose purview is &amp;quot;martial arts&amp;quot; in single combat? <i>Should </i>have I a chance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say a powerful Sidereal grandmaster (as in master of multiple SMA) should have a pretty decent chance. Not an easy win or a guaranteed loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:09:37-07:00","id":635056,"title":"","content":"Personally, I do not expect Omicron's PC to be winning this fight. I expect him to do well. But I expect him to lose. Someday, Hajime might best a Third Circle Demon. I do not think this day is here yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:10:29-07:00","id":635058,"title":"","content":"them be fightin' words, son","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:20:44-07:00","id":635068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a Sidereal be able to defeat a 3CD whose purview is &quot;martial arts&quot; in single combat? Should have I a chance?</div> </div> </div> </div> I would say yes. It's in the Sidereal wheelhouse to be highly skilled martial artists (if not quite having the image of World's Strongest), and I feel it's no fun to be a powerful martial artist if you're not having worthwhile battles with other martial artists. I would, however, at least assume that there's a degree of rules and standards to this; even people challenged to single combat with an actual intention to kill one another can lay down ground rules that establish it more as a duel then a no-holds-barred attempted murder. I think a lone Sidereal would be less suited to other forms of combatent who are less interested in the sport; there are some mean Lunars out there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:33:58-07:00","id":635074,"title":"","content":"Oh god the Viator is so fucking scary. This is on-topic because the Viator is the closest thing to a full Third Circle Demon template we have. I do not think Hajime is going to win. I think our entire Circle would,though. That said <i>holy shit it's base dice pool is equal to my Ending's maximum possible</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 08-21-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:46:18-07:00","id":635077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=635074#post635074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said <i>holy shit it's base dice pool is equal to my Ending's maximum possible</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This is more a comment on how Sidereal dice adders are pretty crappy and how their true strength is TN manipulation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T14:55:33-07:00","id":635081,"title":"","content":"Yeah one of the big power differences between Fenrir's character and mine is that I nabbed all the passive/costless TN reducers I could get and routinely roll attacks at TN 4 and he... doesn't.<br /> <br /> The Viator's honestly kind of underwhelming - not in terms of raw power so much as in his pretty sparse panoply. He mostly crushes you because hugeass mote pool and trololol tick-long perfects, and because nobody paused for a moment to think about what a throwaway line like &quot;tons of all-encompassing spirit charms&quot; actually meant in practice. (hint: it means his unmentioned spirit charms actually contribute far more to his real power level than his Panoply).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:14:30-07:00","id":635092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=635081#post635081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah one of the big power differences between Fenrir's character and mine is that I nabbed all the passive/costless TN reducers I could get and routinely roll attacks at TN 4 and he... doesn't.<br /> <br /> The Viator's honestly kind of underwhelming - not in terms of raw power so much as in his pretty sparse panoply. He mostly crushes you because hugeass mote pool and trololol tick-long perfects, and because nobody paused for a moment to think about what a throwaway line like &quot;tons of all-encompassing spirit charms&quot; actually meant in practice. (hint: it means his unmentioned spirit charms actually contribute far more to his real power level than his Panoply).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah one spirit Charm gets him 63B/55L/24A soak with 38 hardness for 45m. He also eats nine motes every time he deals any damage. Like, you lose nine motes, he gains nine motes.<br /> <br /> Spirit Charms: Actually incredibly fucking broken.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, if one of the 'wide array' of Spirit Charms that he has is Essence Bite, you take Agg damage every time you touch him or he touches you. Oh my god. <i>Aggravated levels which ignore armor.</i> 29m at scene start. 6 aggravated health levels. Every time he touches you or you touch him. Ignoring armor. This means that every time you interact, you take at least one aggravated health level, depending on your natural soak. As a scenelong effect.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":800,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","user":"Fenrir666","date":". 08-21-2015, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T15:41:27-07:00","id":635109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=635092#post635092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah one spirit Charm gets him 63B/55L/24A soak with 38 hardness for 45m. He also eats nine motes every time he deals any damage. Like, you lose nine motes, he gains nine motes.<br /> <br /> Spirit Charms: Actually incredibly fucking broken.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, if one of the 'wide array' of Spirit Charms that he has is Essence Bite, you take Agg damage every time you touch him or he touches you. Oh my god. <i>Aggravated levels which ignore armor.</i> 29m at scene start. 6 aggravated health levels. Every time he touches you or you touch him. Ignoring armor. This means that every time you interact, you take at least one aggravated health level, depending on your natural soak. As a scenelong effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that bad if you're playing straight 2e where you assume any and all attacks of any relevance will be met with a step 2 perfect.<br /> <br /> Doesn't translate well to 2.5. Lethality, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T17:18:22-07:00","id":635196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634861#post634861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys really are underestimating Third Circle Demons. Like...Third Circle Demons are 'fight a full circle of E5 Exalts to a draw/kill several even in a loss.' If their writeups fail to reflect this (spoiler: they do), then they need to be buffed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not the 3CD, it's how widely Exalt power varies. A circle of E5 Whitewolf writeups is basically a joke. But a well-optimized full circle of E5s? That's something entirely different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fenrir666</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=635092#post635092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also, if one of the 'wide array' of Spirit Charms that he has is Essence Bite, you take Agg damage every time you touch him or he touches you. Oh my god. <i>Aggravated levels which ignore armor.</i> 29m at scene start. 6 aggravated health levels. Every time he touches you or you touch him. Ignoring armor. This means that every time you interact, you take at least one aggravated health level, depending on your natural soak. As a scenelong effect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yeah. Where's the fun in spirit charms if you don't deploy that from time to time, especially in 2.5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1628-emeraldstreak","name":"emeraldstreak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1628_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T21:30:41-07:00","id":635430,"title":"","content":"So, is he facing the demon in a humanoid form in an normal duel, or going through the challenges inside the demon in a &quot;36 chambers of shaolin&quot; form?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-21T23:59:55-07:00","id":635485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>danelsan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=635430#post635430\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, is he facing the demon in a humanoid form in an normal duel, or going through the challenges inside the demon in a &quot;36 chambers of shaolin&quot; form?</div> </div> </div> </div>This, this is much more relevant than &quot;does he have Essence Bite,&quot; et cetera.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T02:11:32-07:00","id":635522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=635485#post635485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This, this is much more relevant than &quot;does he have Essence Bite,&quot; et cetera.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a single-combat fight, not a dungeon crawl. I...also don't think it's more relevant. Essence Bite means Hajime loses. Sheathing the Material Form means Hajime loses. Meat of Broken Flesh means Hajime loses. Those three Spirit Charms combine to make Hajime unable to meaningfully do damage, force Hajime to take an aggravated level each exchange, and puts Hajime 18m behind the Viator each time he gets hurt. Nothing is more relevant than 'does he have Essence Bite'.<br /> <br /> That said, we have a freaking fantastic Storyteller, so Suntarankal's gonna have a way better Panoply set-up than the Viator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/800-fenrir666","name":"Fenrir666","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T02:52:56-07:00","id":635540,"title":"","content":"Fenrir I know you're trying to help but as I've pointed earlier I didn't really post this thread to discusss the exact interactions of mechanics that are getting widely houseruled anyway. Yes, Essence Bite is a broken autowin button, so it's probably not going to feature anyway, so no one really cares.<br /> <br /> Yeah, Sun appeared as that affable but incredibly threatening old kung fu master, and the fight will take place against this human form. He doesn't have much choice; backstory shenanigans prevent Third Circles from manifesting their full inhuman forms in Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T04:17:36-07:00","id":635578,"title":"","content":"Something I'm often interested in is how people think the idea of a character, especially a god or demon, with a strong martial arts focus should be expressed through the way that the system and setting handles martial arts. What is most appropriate; a particular martial art, possibly a home-brewed one specific to the character, that encompasses many of the relevant themes (I wonder if this might be a way to reuse something like Cobra Style, although obviously the effort of publishing it would be wasted)? Giving them multiple Styles (at what point do people think that becomes unwieldy)? Giving them spirit Charms that abstract a lot of martial art elements without having to assign one or more particular Styles? On that note, how well should the native powers of such a spirit synergize with any Styles they have, or how much should they have and use things that just don't fit the martial artist image?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T10:22:44-07:00","id":635993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=635578#post635578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> On that note, how well should the native powers of such a spirit synergize with any Styles they have, or how much should they have and use things that just don't fit the martial artist image?</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically to this, I don't think synergy is always appropriate. Supernatural Martial Arts exist completely independently of the existence of a god who represents some facet of the martial arts world. There are any number of such facets. A god of street brawls will benefit more from First Pulse, due to synergy between its innate themes and the themes of the style, but I would expect to see little synergy, and possibly even anti-synergy, between that spirit's own Charms and something like Crane Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":3420,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","user":"Zelbinnean","date":". 08-22-2015, 01:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T10:56:12-07:00","id":636028,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more of the idea of a spirit heavily focused on martial arts having something like Essence Bite. I'm not sure if the premise will even be relevant with how Third Edition is going to approach spirit Charms, though. I'm probably thinking too much in a Second Edition paradigm where you necessarily had to assign Charms based on mechanical utility more than image anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T22:13:30-07:00","id":636687,"title":"","content":"You know what? To hell with all the pessimists. I predict that Hajime will <u><b>totally win!</b></u>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/789-mercury","name":"Mercury","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar789_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-26T21:27:31-07:00","id":641059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=634918#post634918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I never really intended to get into an in-depth discussion of the houserules and homebrew involved in our game (though if people on that forum would find that interesting, I can certainly oblige! I have a bunch to say about people's preconceptions and mistakes about how the balance of the game shakes out in practice, and with/without tweaks). This was really more of a &quot;fun horrible thing that is happening to my character&quot; thread, a bit of &quot;let me tell you about my cool game&quot; chatter, if you will.<br /> <br /> I was also interested in how people felt high-xp Exalts and 3CDs compared but on a more... theoretical, fluff, &quot;this is how it should be&quot; level, rather than strict mechanics.<br /> <br /> My question was never &quot;how screwed am I,&quot; it was more about at which point Exalts raise to such challenges as to make the game's stakes too ridiculous to take seriously.<br /> <br /> <i>Should </i>a Sidereal be able to defeat a 3CD whose purview is &quot;martial arts&quot; in single combat? <i>Should </i>have I a chance?</div> </div> </div> </div>A high-Essence Master of multiple SMA (and potentially high-Essence, custom Throne Shadow Charms)? Hell yeah, you've got a chance! Especially if this isn't all-out Fight To The Death, but a &quot;friendly sparring match&quot;, which means there are rules. The question is, do they favor you or him (and if the latter, then can you bend them the other way)?<br /> <br /> Having said that...Suntarankal is meant to be *damned scary*. I theorize he may even be stronger than Ligier in outright combat (Ligier is a craftsman first and a warrior second, with Sun-kun devotes everything he IS to fighting). <br /> <br /> Since I view him as a demonic Pai Mei (Kill Bill version), I would have a lot of what he does depend on the attitude of your PC and how well he holds to &quot;martial virtues&quot; that Sun-kun holds important (it may even be that THIS, and not your skill, is what he is testing). If you should lose (and you may be expected to, to give Face to your teachers' teacher), but show respect and good grace, then you may get away with a bruising. But if your PC is the loudmouth Arrogant Kung Fu Guy sort, then you can expect a maiming or worse...<br /> <br /> (If I were your ST!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T20:39:26-07:00","id":643720,"title":"","content":"I feel a somewhat important question is WHY your Sid is working with a <i>demon</i>.<br /> <br /> My knowledge of Exalted canon is nowhere near the encyclopedic level of the regulars here, but I'm pretty sure Heaven would disapprove of a Sidereal working with the soul of the very beings it sought to destroy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T21:50:28-07:00","id":643750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=643720#post643720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel a somewhat important question is WHY your Sid is working with a <i>demon</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Sids are under no obligation to not summon demons, only to be mindful that they aren't allowed to set foot in Heaven. Gods are also permitted to summon demons; the Incarnae can even call up the Yozis themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=643720#post643720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My knowledge of Exalted canon is nowhere near the encyclopedic level of the regulars here, but I'm pretty sure Heaven would disapprove of a Sidereal working with the soul of the very beings it sought to destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Heaven&quot; is not this big monolithic hive-mind with a binary &quot;approve/disapprove&quot; switch. It's gonna depend on a hundred or a thousand other factors to give it context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-28T23:07:42-07:00","id":643807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=643750#post643750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. Sids are under no obligation to not summon demons, only to be mindful that they aren't allowed to set foot in Heaven.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't merely summoning a demon as a work slave, this is <i>submitting to one for tutelage</i>.<br /> <br /> If I were a sid and one of my fellow sids was all like &quot;yo I'm taking a trip to Malfeas to learn magic kung-fu from an ungodly powerful demon later losers&quot; I'd wonder why the fuck he isn't learning from a Sidereal sifu when they're explicitly the greatest martial artists of the setting and worry over what demonic shit his master might be teaching him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4801-frostav","name":"Frostav","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T00:38:46-07:00","id":643860,"title":"","content":"Because a Sidereal is under no obligation to teach you, and more importantly, can make you obligated to him. If you're a Gold and he's a Bronze, you might not like the debt he holds over your head; a Sidereal has ways of <i>making</i> demons do things, and the demon can't do shit if you take his teachings and ditch when it comes to reciprocating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T01:28:42-07:00","id":643882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure Heaven would disapprove of a Sidereal working with the soul of the very beings it sought to destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div> People approach demons in their own right more often than they see them as souls of the Yozis. It's dangerous to bring them into Yu-Shan, but binding demons to one's service and learning their secrets is a privilige of the Exalted. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't merely summoning a demon as a work slave, this is submitting to one for tutelage.</div> </div> </div> </div> Why do you not assume that one could use sorcery or Terminal Sanction to bind the demon as an instructor? <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">why the fuck he isn't learning from a Sidereal sifu when they're explicitly the greatest martial artists of the setting</div> </div> </div> </div> That doesn't mean that they know everything. Or that you like them. <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">worry over what demonic shit his master might be teaching him.</div> </div> </div> </div> Do you not think the student would be wary of that as well? To the extent that demons teaching things that turn out to be secretly harmful or whatever is actually the case. It generally isn't; it's more often in their method and personality than in their results. If Ligier makes you something, it's not an evil thing, he just required some form of sacrifice to make it (and might integrate it into a greater sense of trying to win you over to the idea that Creation would be better if it was all in brass and green light).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T05:19:18-07:00","id":643936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=643720#post643720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel a somewhat important question is WHY your Sid is working with a <i>demon</i>.<br /> <br /> My knowledge of Exalted canon is nowhere near the encyclopedic level of the regulars here, but I'm pretty sure Heaven would disapprove of a Sidereal working with the soul of the very beings it sought to destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple, the game is set in Exalted Modern, where the Sidereals work with the Infernal Althing. Many of the specifics of the setting have been changed, but that much remains.<br /> <br /> Also the &quot;submitting for tutelage&quot; is questionable, Hajime has been challenged by Master Sun to a public duel to test his prowess, on the basis that he (Master Sun) taught Hajime's sifu. That is as far as their respectful exchange extends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T12:59:46-07:00","id":644532,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=643720#post643720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel a somewhat important question is WHY your Sid is working with a <i>demon</i>.<br /> <br /> My knowledge of Exalted canon is nowhere near the encyclopedic level of the regulars here, but I'm pretty sure Heaven would disapprove of a Sidereal working with the soul of the very beings it sought to destroy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because he wouldn't take no for an answer, and if I'd refuse his challenge to a duel a week or so down the line, he'd have likely forced the issue by attacking me on the spot, and I wasn't ready to have that fight then.<br /> <br /> Also because my Sidereal had a lot of anger and frustration towards the state of his life at that point, and this offered him a chance to lash out against an acceptable enemy and prove himself to the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-29T14:52:01-07:00","id":644641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Frostav</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=643720#post643720\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel a somewhat important question is why your Sidereal is working with a <i>demon</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals are the Exalted of Martial Arts. You want demons to know styles and techniques the Exalted of Martial Arts don't? You want Hell to be able to point at Heaven and say nanny-nanny-boo-boo?<br /> <br /> Yeah, that's what I thought. Now get out of Omicron's way. He has some green ass to kick.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T10:21:27-07:00","id":675354,"title":"","content":"So, has this duel happened? I'm curious about how it went.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-24T11:51:11-07:00","id":676634,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, we're currently sidetracked into chasing Lyta, who is playing vigilante justice against our &quot;vilain-in-redeeming&quot; PC (and, being Lyta, doing so in an even more evil manner than he ever acted himself), so the timeline is being stretched a bit. Curse the vagaries of the narrative!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T23:20:05-07:00","id":693501,"title":"","content":"This probably falls under Headcanon really, but since we're discussing Suntarankal here...<br /> <br /> *The Crucible of Brass and Iron manifests as a vast complex across many miles of the Demon City, built around a seven-leveled pagoda, within which is the punishing labyrinth of the Forty-Nine Chambers. Most of the Unquestionable allow their component souls their own way in life, but Suntarankal is not so giving. Each floor of his central tower is full of mechanical and environmental hazards, and guarded by one of his Second Circle souls, who pose the final test for each student to ascend to the next level; passing these trials within the Chambers can instantly teach a Charm in a single Style the student is training in. Those who fail any of the tests (which range from physical duels to games of skill or chance to riddle or koan contests) are Banished from the pagoda and must start again, facing new challenges, from the bottom floor. <br /> <br /> Those who pass the final test of Suntarankal's Warden Soul may claim their prize, which always varies with each student. Sometimes it is the final Charm technique of the Style they study, making them masters; other times, it is a demonic Endowment, enabling the student to practice a level of supernatural martial arts beyond that which they normally can. Once, there was a manual which contained the means to reconstruct a Sidereal Martial Art that was otherwise lost to the ages. <br /> <br /> It was this last soul that would brand graduated Masters with the Mark of the Crucible. However, recently (as demons reckon such things), a Sidereal graduate had wise words with the Warden, and put to it a question, that vexed it greatly. This soul soon vanished, beyond the ability of even its Principal to tell where it went or to call it back. Suntarankal is most displeased at this, and has vowed to personally punish the Vizier for their temerity. In the meantime, he has replaced this demon with a powerful Akuma.<br /> <br /> *The most common First Circle Demon created by one of Suntarankal's lesser souls are the Thousand Brassmen. Roughly humanoid figures made of brazen wood, they fulfill their purpose as the primary sparring partners of the Demon City. Showing little initiative, they make poor soldiers, but have an uncanny ability to detect the patterns in an opponents' style, and can even mimic certain charms. The more they spar with a partner, the more they begin to resemble them, until a student is effectively fighting a brass version of herself, even down to her movements and utterances.<br /> <br /> *The Crucible of Brass and Iron can slip through to Creation without being summoned on the occasion when a parent and child fight a formal duel to the death (though they need not know of their relation). One one such occasion, a mortal warrior so impressed him that he allowed her to seduce him, and fathered a powerful Demon-Blooded child. She has since become a master of multiple styles and a destroyer of many dojos, and carves out her legend along the Fighting Tea Road of the Southern Coast (Scroll of Heroes, pg 22). Her father appears to her in her dreams, and she seeks a way to come to him, and claim her ascendancy into true Demon-hood by climbing his tower...<br /> <br /> *Few of the Mortals eking out a poor existence in Malfeas have attained any success or notoriety. Perhaps the greatest is Daron Mason, who was brought to Hell to entertain his masters in gladitorial combat against other Mortal slaves. Tiring of this lifestyle, he escaped, but found life on the Brass City's streets little better. But the demon realm has its own unofficial fighting world, where one may challenge one's limits...<br /> <br /> Demon promoters and trainers liked what they saw in the hardy human, and set him on a harsh regimen of training and treatments that Awakened his Essence and focused his will to survive and win to almost inhuman levels. When they thought he was ready, they sent him to Suntarankal, whose gates welcomed him in, and released him years later, with the brand of Mastery upon him.<br /> <br /> Daron is now a complete Master of First Pulse style, and has gained from the Crucible the ability to combo the charms of that Style. He has since made a name for himself by fighting and winning against First Circle Demon in underground rings, and has become a hero to the desperate Mortals just barely surviving in the cracks of the Demon Realm. He knows this can't last; it is only a matter of time until enforcers of Cecelyne's Law make an example out of him; the best he can hope for is to be made an Akuma for one of the Yozis. He intends to escape to Creation before either happens. <br /> <br /> Maybe those new Green Sun Prince guys can help...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T23:55:12-07:00","id":693507,"title":"","content":"Meh; I don't care how much of a controlling asshole Suntarankal is supposed to be (didn't quite read it that way, myself), your treatment of his Second Circle souls as lockstep Level Bosses disappoints me. <br /> <br /> Gervesin doesn't hang out in Ligier's forges, he's his own person and is off mourning Kinnojo. Makarios doesn't cavort under the shade of the Ebon Dragon, celebrating with Erembour; he's his own person and has a business to run.<br /> <br /> Personally I just wouldn't run it that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T07:36:23-07:00","id":693851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=693507#post693507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh; I don't care how much of a controlling asshole Suntarankal is supposed to be (didn't quite read it that way, myself), your treatment of his Second Circle souls as lockstep Level Bosses disappoints me.<br /> <br /> Gervesin doesn't hang out in Ligier's forges, he's his own person and is off mourning Kinnojo. Makarios doesn't cavort under the shade of the Ebon Dragon, celebrating with Erembour; he's his own person and has a business to run.<br /> <br /> Personally I just wouldn't run it that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That Subordination whatever ability *does* allow a Third Circle Demon to set all his souls to a specific purpose, and there's at least one Demon that has done this in canon, so while it is pretty rare, it CAN happen.<br /> <br /> But if that doesn't work for you here, that's fair, this is just headcanon after all. If you like the idea of his tower having bosses, but don't like them all being his souls, they could easily be mixed up a bit by making them demons from other sources, maybe even a Heroic Serf, and strange things like a Tiend Ghost, a Behemoth, and whatever other weirdness one might find in Hell.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T08:52:29-07:00","id":693893,"title":"","content":"That situation\u2019s a little different, since while the Seven Sorrows are collectively charged with a duty they seem to be going about it in a way that suits each of their roles. So Warden Soul is leading the defences while the Messenger soul is making alliances.<br /> <br /> Here the role is much narrower so it implies that these Second Circle Demons are all of a very similar nature, which in turn makes Suntarankal less interesting if even his Wisdom soul is there to hit things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T09:26:45-07:00","id":693942,"title":"","content":"Super interesting thread, i am Curious to see how it goes honestly-- once you take care of lyta. I agree with lioness re his second circle souls, more than that I don't think a third circle demon should have any problem generating Epic level mooks within his own body, or even spawning unique first circle demons or a race thereof (imagine demons shaped in a mockery of immaculate monks). Anyway, I mostly wanted to comment on the multiple simple charm charm, I think it needs to have restrictions as to what types of charm can be active (unlimited simple attack charms for instance is absurd) I also don't love the ahl cost because I feel like it kind of trivializes the effect and makes using it less exciting. I'd consider something like, pay 1 Limit and roll temporary willpower--&gt; activate a number of scene long charms equal to successes plus 1-&gt; this effect causes character to gain Paradox (sidereal limit is kind of stupid anyway) equal to the failures on the roll, and costs a number of willpower equal to the (successes-failures, minimum 0) on the roll (so if I roll ten dice and 5 come up successes and 5 come up failures it costs 0wp, but if I roll 6 successes and 4 failures I owe 2 wp etc) the cost of which can be reduced by declining to activate more charms than failed dice on the roll (one possible activation that is not taken advantage of reduces cost by 1) id also say that maybe the difficulty of the roll rises by 1 each time it is used in a story but that it can be returned to 0 by performing a significant feat in service to the maidens or your motivation. I know its unsolicited advice and I don't expect you to take it-- just tossing that out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","user":"JiveX","date":". 10-08-2015, 12:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2116-jivex","name":"JiveX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2116_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T11:27:58-07:00","id":694089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/634643-so-my-sidereal-has-been-challenged-to-single-combat?p=693893#post693893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That situation\u2019s a little different, since while the Seven Sorrows are collectively charged with a duty they seem to be going about it in a way that suits each of their roles. So Warden Soul is leading the defences while the Messenger soul is making alliances.<br /> <br /> Here the role is much narrower so it implies that these Second Circle Demons are all of a very similar nature, which in turn makes Suntarankal less interesting if even his Wisdom soul is there to hit things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not necessarily. Each floor of the pagoda can very easily be themed around those 2C roles, as can the direct challenges of the demons themselves. The tests certainly don't have to all be combat-based (although at least one should be); the Wisdom Soul's test can be the game of skill mentioned above, the Messenger's test could be the riddle/koan contest, etc. <br /> <br /> The only thing narrow here would be the space involved to test the students in...and given space-bending weirdness, even *that* doesn't have to be the case! One floor could seem to be an open, unending expanse of desert, snow, whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}